/-!
# Word coordinates for the first marked M₁₂ parabolic

The 64 overlap words, followed by zero, one, or two copies of the cubic actor,
give 192 elements. Their action on twelve points is checked against a finite
table. A decoder of the images of four points proves injectivity; the existing
order of the first parabolic then gives surjectivity. A checked four-generator
transition table supplies multiplication by words without a 192-by-192 table.

These are coordinates in the actual subgroup of the Witt-design M₁₂, with
its original quaternion generators. All tables are untrusted data. The
reconstruction script is `source/generate.py`; each use is kernel checked.
Source: `SmallParabolicPair.Seeds`, following Aschbacher--Smith 14.2.21,
printed p.988. The consumer is the endpoint automorphism construction.
-/

